## Examples (MOST IMPORTANT)
- examples/toolkits/browser_toolkit.py
  - Shows: Creating a ChatAgent with BrowserToolkit for web browsing tasks
  - Key usage: ModelFactory to create models, BrowserToolkit with web_agent_model and planning_agent_model, agent.step() to perform browsing and extract info

- examples/toolkits/pptx_toolkit.py
  - Shows: Creating a ChatAgent with PPTXToolkit for generating PowerPoint presentations
  - Key usage: ModelFactory to create model, PPTXToolkit for slide generation, agent.step() to generate presentation content about CAMEL-AI
  - Includes detailed example of presentation content JSON format and template usage

- examples/agents/single_agent.py
  - Shows: Basic example of creating a ChatAgent with a prompt template and running a step
  - Useful for agent creation pattern

## Implementation
- camel/toolkits/browser_toolkit.py
  - Classes: BaseBrowser, BrowserToolkit
  - BrowserToolkit provides multi-step browser interaction with planning and web agents
  - Methods: browse_url (main browsing method), get_tools (returns toolkit functions)

- camel/toolkits/pptx_toolkit.py
  - Class: PPTXToolkit
  - Provides PowerPoint presentation creation with text formatting, bullet points, images, tables, step-by-step process slides
  - Method: create_presentation (main method to create PPTX file)
  - Uses pptx library and supports image embedding via Pexels API

## Configs and Types
- camel/configs/chatgpt_config.py (implied from usage in examples/toolkits/browser_toolkit.py)
  - ChatGPTConfig for model configuration (temperature, etc.)

- camel/types/enums.py
  - ModelPlatformType (e.g., OPENAI, DEFAULT)
  - ModelType (e.g., GPT_4O_MINI, DEFAULT)

